# 🍇 Grape Leaf Disease Detection: Backend

A Django REST backend that powers an AI-based grape leaf disease detection system. It accepts a leaf image, runs segmentation and disease classification, and returns the result to the frontend.

Built as a minor project for the BEI program at Himalaya College of Engineering (IOE, Tribhuvan University).

> **https://github.com/AJ006-codeland/Minor_Project_Frontend** [add link here]

---

## Overview

Grape farmers often spot diseases late, after the damage has already spread. This backend is the engine behind a tool that lets a user upload a photo of a grape leaf and get a quick diagnosis.

**How it works**

1. The client uploads a leaf image to the API.
2. The backend segments the leaf using the Roboflow API.
3. The segmented leaf goes through a classification model (EfficientNetV2, trained with TensorFlow).
4. The predicted disease and confidence score are returned as JSON and saved to the history.

## Features

- Image upload endpoint for leaf photos
- Leaf segmentation via Roboflow API integration
- Disease classification using a fine-tuned EfficientNetV2 model
- Prediction history stored in the database
- Fully containerised with Docker and Docker Compose
- Secrets kept in environment variables, never in the repo

## Model Performance

| Metric | Result |
| --- | --- |
| Validation accuracy (Phase 1) | ~99% |
| Architecture | EfficientNetV2 |
| Framework | TensorFlow / Keras |

Phase 2 fine-tuning is in progress. Update these numbers when it is done.

## Tech Stack

- **Backend:** Python, Django
- **ML:** TensorFlow, Keras, EfficientNetV2
- **Segmentation:** Roboflow API
- **Containerisation:** Docker, Docker Compose
- **Training:** Google Colab

## Project Structure

```
.
├── backend/            # Django project settings and configuration
├── detector/           # App containing the detection logic and API views
├── manage.py           # Django management script
├── requirements.txt    # Python dependencies
├── Dockerfile          # Image definition for the backend
├── docker-compose.yml  # Service orchestration
└── .env.example        # Template for environment variables
```

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- [Docker](https://www.docker.com/) and Docker Compose
- A [Roboflow](https://roboflow.com/) API key
- Git

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/AJ006-codeland/<your-repo-name>.git
cd <your-repo-name>
```

### 2. Set up environment variables

Copy the example file and fill in your own values:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

```env
SECRET_KEY=your_django_secret_key
DEBUG=True
ROBOFLOW_API_KEY=your_roboflow_api_key
```

> ⚠️ Never commit your real `.env` file. It is listed in `.gitignore`.

### 3. Run with Docker

```bash
docker-compose up --build
```

The API will be available at `http://localhost:8000`.

### Running without Docker

```bash
python -m venv myenv
myenv\Scripts\activate        # Windows
# source myenv/bin/activate   # macOS / Linux

pip install -r requirements.txt
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py runserver
```

## API Usage

> Update the endpoint name below to match your `urls.py`.

**Predict disease from a leaf image**

```http
POST /api/predict/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data
```

| Field | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `image` | file | Photo of a grape leaf |

**Example response**

```json
{
  "disease": "Black Rot",
  "confidence": 0.97
}
```

